is in Established state and has been stable for at least two minutes, with both
routers correctly exchanging one prefix each (200.1.1.0/24 and 195.11.14.0/24
respectively). Both prefixes are installed as active BGP routes in each
router's FIB, and both host default gateways point at their local router
interfaces. There are no iptables firewall rules on either router that would
block forwarded traffic. All physical interfaces across all four devices are
UP/LOWER_UP with correct IP assignments.

The most likely explanation for the reported symptom is that the helpdesk
ticket was filed shortly after the Kathara lab started, during the brief window
(roughly 30–60 seconds) that BGP needs to establish its session and converge
routes before traffic can flow end-to-end. By the time diagnostics were run,
the session had fully converged. No configuration change or corrective action
is required; the network is operating correctly.
